From 185294cfd210ee33948fc2999c3602bacc26cd46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Hugo=20Beauz=C3=A9e-Luyssen?= <hugo.beauzee@datadoghq.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:14:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libstdc++: fix __cpp_lib_chrono for old-ABI-only builds
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The C++20 chrono time zone API is declared when
_GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI || !_GLIBCXX_USE_DUAL_ABI, but
__cpp_lib_chrono only gets its C++20 value when
_GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI is set.  Old-ABI-only builds therefore get
the full API but report the C++17 value.

Widen the condition for the 201907 value to match, and make the
headers check __cpp_lib_chrono instead of repeating the ABI
condition.

Assisted-by: Claude (claude-sonnet-5)

libstdc++-v3/ChangeLog:

	* include/bits/chrono_io.h: Check __glibcxx_chrono for C++20
	tzdb features instead of the ABI macros.
	* include/bits/version.def (chrono): Use extra_cond instead of
	cxx11abi to also define 201907 for old-ABI-only builds.
	* include/bits/version.h: Regenerate.
	* include/std/chrono: Check __cpp_lib_chrono instead of the
	ABI macros.
	* testsuite/lib/libstdc++.exp (check_effective_target_tzdb):
	Replace cxx11_abi check with hosted check and check
	__cpp_lib_chrono in preprocessor condition.
	* testsuite/libstdc++-prettyprinters/chrono.cc: Use
	__cpp_lib_chrono for preprocessor condition and use tzdb for
	effective target.  Remove dg-additional-options.
	* testsuite/std/time/format/data_not_present_neg.cc: Use
	__cpp_lib_chrono for preprocessor conditions and use tzdb for
	effective target.
	* testsuite/std/time/format/empty_spec.cc: Use __cpp_lib_chrono
	for preprocessor conditions.
	* testsuite/std/time/format/nonlocking.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/std/time/format/pr117214.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/std/time/format/pr119517.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/std/time/format/whitespace.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/std/time/hash.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/std/time/syn_c++20.cc: Fix typo in macro name and
	expect new value for !_GLIBCXX_USE_DUAL_ABI.
	* testsuite/std/time/tzdb/1.cc: Require tzdb effective target
	instead of cxx11_abi.
	* testsuite/std/time/tzdb_list/requirements.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/std/time/zoned_time/deduction.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/std/time/zoned_time/io.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/std/time/zoned_time/req_neg.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/std/time/zoned_time/requirements.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/std/time/zoned_traits.cc: Likewise.

Signed-off-by: Hugo Beauzée-Luyssen <hugo.beauzee@datadoghq.com>
Co-authored-by: Jonathan Wakely <jwakely@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit 38523a24316d35ad1b58c162ec422f099fcd77c2)
